From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: kcm: link the Graphics page from Power Management's related pages

The Graphics page (sparky-stereo-graphics) lets the person choose which GPU
a kind of program uses and says that Automatic follows the power profile.
Power Management is where that profile is chosen, so its related pages get
a button to the Graphics page, beside Notifications, Shortcuts, Screen
Locking, Desktop Session and Activities.

The button opens kcm_sparkystereo_graphics through KCMLauncher, as the other
buttons do; the patched PowerDevil package recommends sparky-stereo-graphics.
The string carries no translation here: KDE forks take translations only from
KDE's translation teams, the edition's catalogs are in
sparky-os/translations/powerdevil-graphics-link.po.patch.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
diff --git a/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml b/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
index c95eb3d..3bcb264 100644
--- a/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/GlobalConfig.qml
@@ -373,6 +373,7 @@ Kirigami.ScrollablePage {
                 screenLockingPage.implicitWidth,
                 desktopSessionsPage.implicitWidth,
                 activitiesPage.implicitWidth,
+                graphicsPage.implicitWidth,
             )
 
             MostUsedItem {
@@ -421,6 +422,14 @@ Kirigami.ScrollablePage {
                 Layout.preferredWidth: relatedPagesLayout.maxPageButtonImplicitWidth
                 onClicked: KCM.KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_activities")
             }
+            MostUsedItem {
+                id: graphicsPage
+                kcmIcon: "video-card"
+                kcmName: i18nc("@text:button Name of KCM", "Graphics")
+                Accessible.name: i18n("Open \"Graphics\" settings page")
+                Layout.preferredWidth: relatedPagesLayout.maxPageButtonImplicitWidth
+                onClicked: KCM.KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_sparkystereo_graphics")
+            }
         }
     }
 }
